<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>LegalEase - Local Deployment</title>

  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    body {
      background: #f4f6f9;
      color: #222;
      padding: 30px;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: auto;
    }

    header {
      background: #17365d;
      color: white;
      padding: 30px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    header h1 {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .card {
      background: white;
      padding: 25px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      border-radius: 10px;
      box-shadow: 0 3px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
    }

    h2 {
      color: #17365d;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
    }

    h3 {
      margin: 15px 0 8px;
      color: #2874a6;
    }

    p {
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    ul,
    ol {
      margin-left: 25px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    code {
      background: #eef1f5;
      padding: 3px 6px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      color: #c0392b;
    }

    pre {
      background: #1e1e1e;
      color: #eee;
      padding: 18px;
      border-radius: 7px;
      overflow-x: auto;
      margin: 12px 0;
    }

    .success {
      background: #eaf7ea;
      border-left: 5px solid #27ae60;
      padding: 15px;
      margin-top: 15px;
    }

    .folder {
      background: #f8f9fa;
      padding: 15px;
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
      border-radius: 7px;
      margin-top: 10px;
      font-family: monospace;
      white-space: pre;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

  <header>
    <h1>LegalEase</h1>
    <p>EPIC 5: Deployment – Local Deployment Preparation</p>
  </header>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>1. Deployment Objective</h2>

    <p>
      The objective of this deployment setup is to prepare the
      LegalEase application for running locally on a developer's
      computer without requiring a production server.
    </p>

    <div class="success">
      The application can be tested locally using a browser and
      a lightweight local development server.
    </div>
  </div>


  <div class="card">
    <h2>2. Project Structure</h2>

    <p>Recommended LegalEase project structure:</p>

    <div class="folder">
LegalEase/
│
├── index.html
├── css/
│   └── style.css
├── js/
│   └── app.js
├── assets/
│   └── images/
└── README.md
    </div>
  </div>


  <div class="card">
    <h2>3. Local Requirements</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Windows, macOS or Linux computer</li>
      <li>Modern web browser</li>
      <li>Visual Studio Code or any code editor</li>
      <li>Optional: Node.js for local development server</li>
      <li>Internet connection for optional external resources</li>
    </ul>
  </div>


  <div class="card">
    <h2>4. Local Deployment Using Browser</h2>

    <p>
      For a simple static version of LegalEase, the application
      can be opened directly from the project folder.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>Open the LegalEase project folder.</li>
      <li>Locate <code>index.html</code>.</li>
      <li>Double-click the file.</li>
      <li>The application will open in the default browser.</li>
      <li>Test the document preview and export functionality.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>


  <div class="card">
    <h2>5. Local Deployment Using VS Code</h2>

    <p>
      The recommended development method is to use Visual Studio Code
      with a local development extension such as Live Server.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>Open Visual Studio Code.</li>
      <li>Select <b>File → Open Folder</b>.</li>
      <li>Select the LegalEase project folder.</li>
      <li>Open <code>index.html</code>.</li>
      <li>Start the local development server.</li>
      <li>Open the generated localhost address in the browser.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Example Local Address</h3>

    <pre>http://127.0.0.1:5500/</pre>
  </div>


  <div class="card">
    <h2>6. Deployment Using Node.js</h2>

    <p>
      If Node.js is installed, a lightweight local HTTP server
      can be used to serve the application.
    </p>

    <h3>Check Node.js</h3>

    <pre>node --version</pre>

    <h3>Start Local Server</h3>

    <pre>npx serve .</pre>

    <p>
      After starting the server, open the localhost URL shown
      in the terminal.
    </p>
  </div>


  <div class="card">
    <h2>7. Local Testing Checklist</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Application loads successfully.</li>
      <li>Navigation works correctly.</li>
      <li>Legal document form accepts user input.</li>
      <li>Dynamic preview updates correctly.</li>
      <li>Print/PDF functionality works.</li>
      <li>JSON export works.</li>
      <li>Responsive layout works on smaller screens.</li>
      <li>No major browser console errors are present.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>


  <div class="card">
    <h2>8. Deployment Status</h2>

    <div class="success">
      <strong>Local Deployment Ready</strong>
      <p>
        LegalEase is structured as a locally deployable frontend
        application and can be tested using a browser or local
        development server.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
